cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use emem, cite the software when you ran it and the preprint when you
  build on the protocol. They are separate artefacts: the repository is the
  running implementation, the preprint is the design and the evidence.
title: "emem: shared, verifiable memory for AI agents"
abstract: >-
  A content-addressed memory protocol for AI agents. One place has one address,
  one observation has one signed fact, and a citation resolves to byte-identical
  signed bytes that any receiver verifies offline without trusting the sender.
type: software
